# Direct messages

The product label is «Сообщения». Do not rename the header envelope to «Переписки». The conversation list does not show a «Сообщения» heading. The trainer cabinet sidebar and the plain-user account sidebar both say «Мои сообщения». The admin sidebar stays «Сообщения».

The full file map and edit checklist are in `.cursor/skills/trenio-messages/SKILL.md`. Product behavior stays in `docs/TECH_SPEC.md` §4.6.

## Who may talk

- One open conversation per pair of accounts. A client and a card owner share one thread. The portal welcome is that same pair: the trainer's account and `trenioby`, stored with `host_user_id` and no card. Opening the card reuses that thread instead of creating a second empty one. An empty duplicate of the pair is deleted. No user-to-user chat. Questions to the portal go to the admin account `trenioby`. That thread has no trainer card.
- A client starts a thread at `/account/messages`. A trainer or club stays in `/me/messages` for both client threads and threads they start with another profile. `/account/messages` redirects those roles to `/me/messages` and keeps the conversation id. Staff open `/admin/messages` on the «Переписки (N)» tab, every conversation on the site. «Жалобы (N)» is the second tab. Staff do not write in a thread unless they are a participant. The profile direct icon opens that trainer's dialog: a client at `/account/messages?trainer=`, a trainer or club at `/me/messages?trainer=`, and staff at `/admin/messages?trainer=` on «Переписки» with that dialog open. A staff visit to `/account/messages` follows the same path and does not land on `/admin`.
- Catalog trainer cards (home, categories, cities, search, map, favorites, and similar trainers) do not show a phone, Instagram, or Telegram icon. After the bookmark they show the outline plane. It opens the same thread as «Написать», in a new tab, and a click by someone other than the owner is counted. Hide it when the slug is in `messaging.ownedSlugs`. A guest’s plane goes to login and returns to the same thread. The city, sports, price, and rating stay. The given name and surname are two lines, 14px from 768px and 13px below, and are not cut off. Sports on the card are text. A sport link belongs only on a public profile tag. The profile block after reviews («Как со мной связаться») uses icon links: a phone handset, Instagram, Telegram, and a direct message. The direct mark is one outline plane in a coral rounded square the same size as Instagram and Telegram. The plane stays inside that square and does not cross the rounded edge. Hover moves the disc. A click by someone other than the owner is counted with the phone, Instagram, and Telegram clicks. The inbox mark stays an envelope with rounded corners and a curved flap. There is no email icon. Instagram, Telegram, and the direct message open in a new tab. The handset is a `tel:` link and stays on this page. On the profile the formatted number sits beside the handset. Hide the direct icon when the slug is in `messaging.ownedSlugs`. A guest’s direct icon goes to login and returns to the same thread.
- The owner or staff may close a thread. A participant may delete the thread for themselves from «…», after a confirmation. That copy leaves their list. The other participant keeps the history and sees «Переписка была удалена пользователем» when at least one message from before that clear is still visible to them. An empty thread that was opened and then deleted does not appear for the other account: no row and no sentence. Until a message exists, only the account that opened the thread sees it. The row is removed for everyone only when an account is deleted.
- A blocked pair cannot send. A profile must be published. The portal admin is the exception: a new trainer account gets one welcome from the admin user `trenioby` (`trenioby@gmail.com`), and the same thread stays open for questions. There is no trainer profile and no `/trainers/trenioby` page. The database rejects that slug. Admin and superadmin accounts do not get that welcome. The letter text is the site setting `trainer_welcome`, edited at `/admin/site`.
- One user may message at most 10 different trainers per Europe/Minsk calendar day. The 11th is refused in a `CabinetNotice` popup. Repeating a trainer already messaged that day is allowed. Count the initiator's sent messages, not the owner's replies.

## Text and chrome

- Count visible graphemes with `reviewTextLength` after `sanitizeReviewHtml`. The initiator's first message is 1000. Later messages are 4000. Stored HTML may be 12000 (`messages_body_len`). A body of only format characters, such as zero-width spaces, is empty.
- The list has a search field with a magnifying-glass icon. From two characters it matches the other person's name and the message text. A given name or surname still matches when the layout was Latin, Latin and Cyrillic lookalikes were mixed, the space was skipped, or one letter was swapped, added, or missing. The same rules as the catalog sport and city field (`query-flex`) decide that. The query is not written to `app_logs`.
- «Ответить» is a reply arrow beside the bubble, not a text link. It quotes one message in the same thread (`messages.reply_to_id`). The quote inside the bubble and the bar above the field are one short muted line with a left stroke, without a heading. The quote does not widen the bubble. The message that was quoted uses a slightly deeper bubble color. «Изменить» is a pencil icon on that bubble. It rewrites the sender's own text for 15 minutes, sets `edited_at`, and leaves the list order as it is. The bubble then says «изменено».
- The composer is one rounded row: a paperclip, the field, an emoji button, and a round send button. There is no formatting toolbar and the screen does not explain inline styles. A quote or an edit shows a bar above that row. The counter appears only near the limit. A paperclip attaches up to 9 files, each at most 5 MB (`5242880` in `message_attachments_size`): JPEG, PNG, WEBP, GIF, and PDF. The bytes decide the type. An image that cannot be decoded is refused and removed from disk. Files stay in `data/message-files/` and are served only to someone who can read the thread (`/messages/files/{id}`). A photo also stores a JPEG preview. The bubble shows a 72px thumbnail, and a tap opens the full image on the same page with rotate-left and rotate-right. Client bubbles are turquoise and trainer bubbles are coral. The viewer’s own bubbles stay on the right. Ctrl+V or ⌘V pastes a screenshot into the draft. Enter sends the text already visible in the field. Shift+Enter inserts a line break. A run of breaks collapses to one blank line, and the field keeps at most 200 breaks, so a million enters cannot grow the draft or the stored HTML. Holding Enter does not send a burst. Ctrl+Enter or ⌘+Enter still sends. A participant may mark the other person's message with a thumb (`message_reactions`, one row per account and message). The mark is a stroke thumb, brand-colored when it is on, and a second press removes it. The sender cannot mark their own message. Apply the table with `npm run messages:install`. A message may be attachments only.
- A participant reports the whole thread once, from «…» in the thread header and the menu item «Пожаловаться». The dialog asks for a reason and a comment (1000 graphemes). The client and the trainer each file their own row. The row is `message_reports`: `conversation_id`, `reporter_side` (`client` or `trainer`), Russian `reason`, and `comment`. `message_id` stays empty. A second report from the same person is a duplicate. Active admins get mail with the reason and comment, not the chat. Staff read the row at `/admin/messages`. Do not write the comment into `app_logs`. «Заблокировать» is the next menu item and asks for confirmation first. A portal welcome is a thread with the admin and has no trainer card. Report, block, and delete are absent there, and the server refuses all three. «Удалить диалог» follows it and asks for confirmation. `deleteConversationForViewer` sets `user_deleted_at` for the client or `peer_deleted_at` for the profile owner or the portal host, and clears that side's revive stamp. Messages stay in the database. The other side keeps them. A thread with no visible message stays off the other account's list, and `deletedByCounterpart` stays false, so the sentence is not shown on an empty draft. Opening the same person again sets `user_revived_at` or `peer_revived_at` and brings the empty draft back for that account only. A message sent after the clear brings the thread back without the older text. Deleting again hides that newer text too. Search and the unread total skip text at or before the viewer's stamp. The journal action is `message.clear` and stores no message body. Apply the columns with `npm run messages:install`. The row is `blocked_pairs`: the client account and that trainer profile. Either side stops: the client and the trainer. The account stays active, and dialogs with other trainers stay open. Staff can block the same pair. While the pair is blocked, «Разблокировать» sits in the middle of that thread and asks for confirmation before the row is removed and the thread opens again. The menu labels stay 14px and regular weight. The field shows «Написать сообщение» as a placeholder, not as text in the field.
- On a phone the list and the open thread are separate steps. The thread fills the screen under the sticky header, and «К списку» returns to the list. The phone's own back button does the same: the first press shows the dialog list, and the next one leaves the messages page. If that back would open a page outside the dialog list, the list is pushed on top of it. A dialog opened from a profile, a notification, or a fresh tab keeps that list behind it. Do not auto-open the first row on a narrow screen.
- Emoji are written into the editor value (insert a text node, then dispatch `input`). The picker includes every skin tone and the vulgar group.
- The sender sees «Доставлено» after the server stores the message, and «Прочитано» when the other participant's `last_read_message_id` is at least that id. That cursor moves when the bottom edge of the message enters the visible log. The same edge is the cutoff on a phone, a tablet, and a wide screen. Opening the thread does not mark a message that still hangs below it. A participant marks it, including the portal welcome in the admin cabinet. A staff reader who is not in the thread does not. A reply marks the thread read through that reply, and the header, the menu, and the dialog row lose that unread count. An unowned profile stays «Доставлено». Every conversation row, for every role, shows that same state of its latest message in the right corner: one check is delivered, two checks are read.
- The messages icon is an envelope. The reviews icon stays a speech bubble. Sidebar counts for favorites, reviews, likes, and messages are small muted numbers at 11px. The messages number uses the brand color when it is not zero, because that number is the unread total. Nested cabinet counts stay muted. The header profile mark is a link to that role's cabinet home and has no menu. It stays below 768px, without the nickname. On a phone the site menu opens the same cabinet list, and each item uses the same line icon as that cabinet's sidebar. When a trainer, a club, or a plain user has unread messages, the burger and the nickname in the site menu show a very small brand-colored exclamation mark. Staff do not. For every role the envelope, the site menu, and the cabinet sidebar share one unread total (`own + inbox`): messages someone else sent to this account that this account has not opened, including threads the trainer started. A message this account sent stays out of that total. On the staff list a row badge counts the same incoming unread, and only when this account is a participant. «Переписки (N)» stays the number of conversations. New reports stay on «Жалобы (N)» and are not that badge.
- The list is ordered by latest activity. On a wide screen the first visit with no conversation in the URL opens the first row. After the X hides the thread, the list stays as it is until a row is chosen. A row highlights on hover, and the open row stays highlighted. A `?trainer=` link resolves that card's existing dialog, or creates it, and opens that id. The newest row is not substituted while that lookup is in flight.
- In a dialog the given name and surname are one line. Do not label the thread «Открыта» or «Закрыта». The composer uses 14px text on a wide screen and 16px on a phone, so the system keyboard does not zoom the page.
- The portrait is the published card photo when that account has one, otherwise the account photo. A published name opens `/trainers/{slug}` in a new tab and uses the same new-tab mark as the cabinet identity. A plain account name stays text. When the header shows the client, «Тренер: …» opens that thread's card in a new tab with the same mark.
- On a phone the thread slides in under the header on a white sheet. The sheet slides in, and the top edge stays under the header. A new bubble, the typing line, the quote bar, and the menu ease in. Reduced motion turns those fades off. The pane itself does not jump. «К списку», a swipe from the left edge, and the phone's own back button return to the list. The next phone back leaves the messages page. There are no previous or next arrows in that header: they covered the name, and the next thread is opened from the list. A wide screen still shows those arrows. The composer rises above the keyboard. Block and report stay in the «…» menu.
- On a wide screen the X hides the open thread. It does not mark the conversation closed and does not show «Открыть». The row stays in the list. The page does not open the first row again after that.
- Admin and superadmin cabinets use `.layout-staff` (1680px). Trainer and account cabinets stay on 1240px.

## Live updates

The open page keeps one websocket at `/messages/live`. The upgrade accepts the session cookie only when `Origin` is this site (`trenio.by`, `www.trenio.by`, `trenio.local`, or `appOrigin()`). A missing or foreign origin is refused. `127.0.0.1` and `localhost` are allowed only when `NODE_ENV` is not production. A thread event tells both participants and staff readers to reload that dialog and the list. An unread event refreshes the header count for participants only. A cabinet event asks that person's open pages to pull likes, favorites, statistics, and the cabinet counters. The event carries no counts. The same counters stay in the header menu and in the trainer, user, and admin sidebars. The other participant sees «печатает…» while this account is typing; that signal is not logged and is not shown to staff who are only reading. Writes stay the existing POST functions. The socket carries no message text.

If the socket drops, the page reconnects after 1s, 2s, 4s, then at most every 15s, and refreshes the open dialog every 20s until the socket is back. Returning to a visible tab refreshes once. A hidden tab does not refresh. A refused session stops the socket.

Opening a thread pins the log to the bottom when the unread tail fits in the pane. When that tail is taller than the pane, scroll to the top of the oldest unread message so a long message starts at its first line. A message the viewer just sent still pins to the bottom. A staff reader who is not a participant stays at the bottom.

The message email, Telegram, and the browser push go out only when that person is offline. A green dot means a visible tab in the last minute. An orange dot means the tab is hidden, they switched browser, or they were here within ten minutes. A gray dot is offline. While they are green or orange, the letter waits and checks again. The waiting letter and the waiting browser notice are rows in `message_notices`, so a process restart still sends them. `npm run messages:install` creates that table and widens the file check to 5 MB. The message email goes only to a verified mailbox, and only when «Сообщения» is on. Telegram goes to either participant when that account has a chat id and has already opened the bot or the Mini App. The note has no message text. Email and Telegram wait two quiet minutes. A browser notification waits 15 quiet seconds, then the same offline check as the letter, and goes out once that person is offline, on a computer, a phone, or the installed app, while `users.push_messages` is on (default true). The cabinet row is «В браузере» in the «Уведомления» card, and it wraps on a narrow screen. The browser still asks once, on the first tap, because the system permission needs a gesture. There is no separate opt-in strip. A focused tab skips the system banner and shows «Вам написали» with the sender name and «Открыть». The banner text has no message body. Turning the switch off deletes that account's subscriptions. The Mini App uses the Telegram note instead, because that web view cannot show a system push. The staff report letter does not use that switch.

```ts
// wrong: raw HTML length, or the wide staff grid on a trainer page
if (input.body.length > 500) throw new Error("too long");

// right: visible characters, Russian AuthError, staff width only around /admin
if (reviewTextLength(html) > limit) {
  throw new AuthError("Первое сообщение тренеру — не длиннее 1000 символов.", "VALIDATION");
}
```

Server writes stay in `src/lib/messages/functions.ts` with `POST` and `requireAuthMiddleware`. `beforeLoad` is not the security boundary.
